Title: Distribution of molecular subtypes in a Colombian cohort of patients with acute lymphoblastic leukemia using whole-transcriptome analysis.
Abstract: Acute lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL) is a common pediatric malignancy and shows marked genetic heterogeneity. Transcriptomic profiling may improve molecular diagnosis and risk stratification, particularly in admixed Latin American populations.

